STYLE="""MISE EN MONSTRE game art direction: charming spooky subterranean kitchen fantasy; ultra-low-poly flat-shaded forms built from reusable primitives, chunky silhouettes, matte solid color fields, a few bold edge highlights. Small faceless chefs with two warm ivory eyes, oversized off-white chef hats, colored sleeves and simple mitten hands. Olive, parchment cream, warm amber firelight against cool deep teal. Stylized readable stone, wood, brass and cooking props. Food-like mess, never realistic gore. NO photorealism, realistic fur, detailed skin, intricate engraved ornament, microtexture, cinematic realism or high-fantasy armor overload. Shape and silhouette carry the design. These are visual proposals, not claims of implemented content."""
COOKBOOK="""Create a landscape 3:2 polished visual development sheet showing TWO LARGE FLAT PARCHMENT COOKBOOK PAGES side by side. Thin olive cover rim and narrow sewn brown centre. This is an easy-to-read practical handbook, cute and sparse. Left: monster field note about the PICKLE MIMIC, a chunky angular jar containing a green pickle creature with two ivory eyes; include one clear sound cue, one safe/unsafe interaction cue and a tiny ingredient or footprint note. Right: TOMB-TRUFFLE BROTH, four huge pictorial preparation steps SIMMER / COVER / OFF HEAT / BRINE + HERBS. Pot, cloche, truffle, brine jar and herb icons. Picture-first and gameplay-readable; short headings only, no tiny prose. At least half the visual information should be simple silhouettes and symbols. Add a small isolated matching sticker/stamp/button-tab row beneath the spread. Keep page content flat graphic rather than a realistic illustration printed inside a photoreal book. Show the distinct design approach in every panel."""
ENV="""Create a landscape 3:2 ENVIRONMENT ART DIRECTION DIPTYCH: left panel labelled ART DIRECTION is a readable regular environment concept; right panel labelled PLAYER VIEW shows THE SAME place from a standing chef's eye height around1.65m, with convincing darkness and a small warm lantern/torch light pool. Both panels share the same modular architecture, landmark and mechanism. Do not substitute an aerial view for the player panel. Tiny ochre sleeve/mitten and held lantern at the lower edge, no HUD. Dark areas remain dark, but critical floor edges, route silhouettes and the local clue can be read. Use broad flat-shaded faceted surfaces; NOT realistic masonry and texture noise. Make it look like a beautiful stylized playable game, not a photograph. Environment dressing must respect the supplied topology and elevation, not invent new connecting routes. Study one distinct place with clear foreground/midground/background."""
INTRO="""Create a landscape 3:2 SIX-PANEL cinematic intro storyboard, arranged three columns and two rows, numbered01 to06. Preserve one coherent cast and setting through all panels. Royal Daily Feast premise: King Cloche is a round faceless ruler under a golden serving-cloche crown with two ivory eyes and a red ceremonial robe; the tall thin Majordomo wears a long black-and-cream chef livery and carries an order parchment; the Royal Taster has an ochre herbal apron and spoon; the little teal Bell Page carries a handbell. The player crew are scrappy faceless low-poly cooks. Use strong staging, expressive poses and simple prop comedy; very little text, no speech paragraphs. Establish the royal dish demand, show why the cooks descend below, then hand into first-person expedition play. The six frames must form a different actual opening sequence, not six unrelated mood pictures. Story and lore extensions are optional proposals, not new canon."""
HUD="""Create a landscape 3:2 complete GAMEPLAY HUD CONCEPT BOARD. Upper75percent contains one large16:9 player-view screenshot mockup in a dark flat-shaded dungeon kitchen, kept readable with warm lamp light and a chef's gloved hand at the bottom. Design ALL HUD elements as one coherent parchment-paper graphic language. Include a compact dish objective tracker with ingredient icons and collection/preparation/return progress; a four-player party tracker with colored faceless chef icons, microphone/voice states and own vital strip; a transient parchment notification reading 'A contraption has moved'; a quiet centre reticle and one contextual interaction prompt; compact item slots and held-item hints. Keep the centre60percent mostly clear and avoid huge MMO panels. Lower25percent shows enlarged matching button glyphs, prompt styles, party microphone speaking/muted states, notification and objective states. Short legible labels only. Show a book-open context sample in the component strip: Q PREVIOUS, E NEXT, LMB CLOSE, plus R HOLD THROW in the held-item context. Use meaningful shapes as well as colors. No modern glassmorphism, neon, glossy smartphone UI, mana/XP meters or invented currency. These are art/layout proposals, not an implemented HUD."""
MECHANISM="""Create a landscape 3:2 LEVEL MECHANISM / EXPEDITION CLUE design board. A large central low-poly prop assembly and a wide first-person in-level placement view. Small clear panels show missing/unreadable state, discovery, and assembled/activated state with shape arrows. Include two ways of communicating direction: a clearer interpretation and a more obscure environmental interpretation, both physically plausible. Essential clues must remain legible at player height in a local lantern light pool. Mechanisms should feel carved, repaired, cooked-on and handled, with chunky readable silhouettes and very few materials. Avoid futuristic UI, laser puzzles, magical floating objective arrows or unreadably tiny carved text. For fragment puzzles, orientation must be unambiguous and progress visible; do not require two players holding inputs simultaneously or permanently block a sole exit. Show the player action and resulting physical change rather than a decorative prop alone."""
MONSTER="""Create a landscape 3:2 PROTOTYPE MONSTER concept board. One large clear full-body three-quarter design, a small side silhouette, three tiny behavior beats, and a large bottom player-eye encounter view in a dark modular kitchen dungeon with a warm lantern light pool. Give the monster a memorable, simple, buildable low-poly silhouette distinct from a chef. Communicate a readable warning tell before danger, one simple trigger/response, and a visible counterplay. Show scale with a small faceless chef. Indicate eye visibility, an audible cue and a physical trace through actual images rather than dense text. Sparse short labels only. Slow dread, route choices, food/cooking associations; no realistic gore or action-boss spectacle. A monster must not permanently seal the only route."""
VERMIN="""Create a landscape 3:2 CUTE DUNGEON VERMIN design board. Four clearly separated labelled columns show PANTRY RAT, SOOTLING, FLOUR PUFF and LINT SCUTTLER. Each has a large different low-poly silhouette, a smaller behavior pose and a scale cue. Bottom third is a broad player-eye vignette placing all four tiny creatures in the same dark kitchen/pantry corner with warm lantern or oven light. Rats look like angular rodents, not hooded chefs; sootlings are little black faceted coal puffs, flour puffs are ivory angular dust clouds, lint scuttlers are bundles of scraps with tiny legs. Ivory eye dots where appropriate; expressiveness through body pose and broad shapes, not realistic fur. Approximate sizes10-25cm. Harmless or optional interaction proposals, not mandatory threats or quest-gating. No realistic animal suffering or gore. Short captions only; show the proposed interaction with crumb, hand, jar or props. Do not replace all four species with palette swaps of one body."""

jobs=[]
def add(category,prefix,number,title,brief,notes,base,**extra):
    ident=f'{prefix}-{number:02}'
    item={'id':ident,'category':category,'number':number,'title':title,'brief':brief,'notes':notes,
          'status':'pending','image':f'images/{category}/{ident}-{slug(title)}.png',**extra}
    item['prompt']=f'{STYLE}\n\n{base}\n\nSPECIFIC DIRECTION {ident} - {title}: {brief}\n\nOnly tiny board identifier {ident} at the top; prioritize the art itself.'
    (ROOT/'images'/category).mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    jobs.append(item)

books=[
 ('Apprentice margin doodles','Loose bold charcoal-ink doodles, confident uneven hand lettering, one sage ink wash, a tiny red warning stamp and a single pasted silhouette sticker. Cream paper remains mostly empty. Monster listening bell and four cooking cards have very thick simple strokes.','Baseline sparse notebook: quickest icon read; compare against the more assembled paper systems.'),
 ('Sticker recipe club','Oversized friendly cut-paper stickers with visible white cut edges; monster jar, big pot, cloche and herb sticker. Rounded torn rectangles, tiny handwritten corrections, a deliberately crooked warning sticker, simple visual checklist. No realistic food painting.','Separate sticker art can be reused across recipe, bestiary and notifications.'),
 ('Kitchen rubber stamps','Two-ink linocut/rubber-stamp language: black chunky silhouette stamps plus olive or red progress marks. Imperfect stamped edges but huge clean shapes. Monster anatomy expressed in three shapes; cooking stages in four square stamp blocks.','Very limited palette and reusable stamps; a stamped check can distinguish tested knowledge.'),
 ('Grease pencil corrections','Soft dark grease-pencil circles, underlines and broad arrows on flat warm cream. Smudges are a few graphic marks, not noisy texture. Tiny chef mitten doodle crosses out heating the brine; bold squiggle steam and a marginal question mark.','The book feels used by cooks; annotations remain secondary to the four big action icons.'),
 ('Pinned kitchen tickets','Torn order tickets pasted into an otherwise empty notebook: one large monster silhouette ticket, two narrow sound/counterplay tickets, four sequential recipe ticket cards. Red twine corner, one brass paper pin, warm sage tape.','Modular ticket blocks accommodate unfinished recipes without filling the spread with prose.'),
 ('Sewn patch notebook','Flat cloth patches sewn onto paper: monster silhouette patch, broad hand-drawn diagrams and four folded instruction flaps held with a few giant stitches. Almost no shading. Olive and biscuit colors. Tabs resemble repaired apron scraps.','A tactile textile option matching chef aprons; keep stitch count low for readability.'),
 ('Pictogram trail','Near-wordless travel-guide clarity: each page has one oversized hero pictogram and a thick arrow trail linking simple action icons. Four numbered cooking circles, sound waves and stop-hand icons for the jar creature. Cream/black/olive only.','Strong picture-first option; external captions retain exact instructions rather than relying on generated text.'),
 ('Shadow puppets and speech bubbles','Adorable black silhouette jar monster with ivory eyes, flat cut-out chef mitten acting as narrator, hand-cut sage speech bubbles containing only symbols like bell, pause and X. Four big theatrical cooking silhouettes.','Uses the same expressive face language as the characters while keeping pages simple.'),
 ('Napkin scrap scrapbook','Large cream napkin and brown-paper scraps taped onto parchment, one-color marker drawings, a few grease-ring circles, ingredient-sticker labels, wide whitespace. Monster is a cheeky scribble with an oversized jar lid.','Domestic and scrappy; avoid decoration reducing the actual diagram area.'),
 ('Scout route annotations','Cooking arrows resemble a hand-drawn route through four stations; monster note uses big footstep dots and a bell radius doodle. One folded paper clue, compass-free directional strokes, broad pencil lines and sage markers.','Connects field observation to cooking procedure without turning the recipe into a literal minimap.'),
 ('Kitchen comic strips','Four clean comic panels for the dish, expressive faceless-chef mitten acting out each step; monster page has a three-panel sound/reveal/wait gag. Huge black outlines, tiny flat halftone patches, cream paper with one red accent.','Sequential action can teach order; keep every panel readable at the equipped-book scale.'),
 ('Nope and yep field cards','Big paired NOPE / YEP icon cards on the monster page: smashing a jar crossed out, waiting/quiet marked yes. Recipe uses four large rounded cards with hand-drawn check marks and tiny ingredient stickers. Childlike confident art without baby styling.','Good/bad examples emphasize preserving an ingredient and avoiding a common cooking mistake.'),
]
for i,(title,brief,notes) in enumerate(books,1):add('cookbook','CB',i,title,brief,notes,COOKBOOK)

zones={
 'B':[
 ('Arrival Hall and hoist','Top arrival landing at+10m, looking into one deep shaft. A simple enormous wooden hoist above is the landmark; distant amber Pit glow is below. Huge square timbers, cream wayfinding cloth and teal void.','hall'),
 ('The Great Stair','Clockwise descending inner helix wraps the same shaft in wide simple stone flights; show at least three landings at different heights and an outer service stair glimpsed through a side doorway. Do not flatten the helix into a horizontal corridor.','landingNE'),
 ('Charnel Court balcony','Court at+7.5m with its lit red-key balcony overlooking the same shaft. Broader welcoming kitchen-court silhouette, stacked pots and a warm plinth. Frame the key as a small red shape cue, not a floating objective icon.','court'),
 ('Ossuary bone pantry','Ossuary at+5m, a long pantry of broad bone-shaped shelf braces and ceramic storage niches. A pack plinth is physically recognizable; the next landing can be seen through a deliberate opening.','ossuary'),
 ('Reliquary brass shelves','Reliquary at+2.5m: compact gold-brass containers, covered serving dishes and one quiet altar-like food shelf. Warm objects cluster in one pool; the doorway turns away from the shaft into darkness.','reliquary'),
 ('Chime Hall landing','Chime Hall at0m. Three huge suspended kitchen bells form the identity, with a raised path and simple dial/lever hardware. Through the doorway retain the shaft landmark and a reading angle on glyphs.','chime'),
 ('Salt Cellar strata','Salt Cellar at-2.5m, horizontal low pale salt strata, broad shallow alcoves and little brine channels. A simple chain or channel leads the eye to the wheel route; chunky cream mineral shapes, dark olive doors.','cellar'),
 ('Pump Room machinery','Pump Room at-5m: one big wood-and-brass wheel and a heavy piston, with a dry floor channel as the mechanism tell. Machine silhouette clear enough to name from a doorway. Avoid a maze of decorative pipes.','pump'),
 ('Cistern lowest water','Cistern at-7.5m, shallow still teal water with a readable stone rim and low hanging square lamps. Reflections are broad simple patches; wet paths and dry pack-rest spots remain distinct.','cistern'),
 ('Smokehouse ember room','Smokehouse at0m with a tall soot-black chimney volume, hanging broad cured-food silhouettes and dim orange embers. A warm vent stripe contrasts the shaft teal outside. No realistic animal carcasses.','smokehouse'),
 ('Brine Larder support stop','Brine Larder at-7.5m: one large brine vat, drying rack, clear pack plinth and two preparation shelves. Art communicates a deliberate support stop rather than generic loot shelving.','larder'),
 ('The Pit and earned return','Pit at-7.5m, huge low cavern and monster traces beside the return lift. Show the tiny lit hoist above as the vertical compass, and a readable scout ladder/closet exit at the rim. Vault doorway is a heavy sealed shape, not a new route.','lair')],
 'C':[
 ('The Well on the first bank','Two Towers and the Canal layout. The hoist/Well forms one landmark on the first bank; the Bell Tower across the canal forms a second. Main floor at0m, broad dark water divides the composition.','rimN'),
 ('Belfry on the other bank','Belfry on the opposite bank, bell lantern silhouette visible across dark water. A red key hangs under the bell on the loft. Frame it through the tower opening at player height, not an overhead map.','belfry'),
 ('Bone Bridge crossing','A narrow elevated Bone Bridge at+2.5m crosses the canal between two banks. Use chunky bone-white beams and a memorable low arch. Both the hoist and bell silhouettes orient the player; no extra crossings.','bridgehead'),
 ('The Ford','The Ford offers a lower shallow crossing at-2.5m rising toward0m on the other side. Round stepping edges, shin-deep broad teal water, a warm light beyond the bend. Clearly different silhouette from the bridge above.','ford-w'),
 ('Chain Crossing and sluice','A heavy chain causeway controlled by a sluice hand-wheel. The physical chain runs along the Cellar floor toward the wheel and the barred Pump end. Show slack/taut chain states as an art cue, no new puzzle logic.','sluice'),
 ('Ossuary pack plate','Ossuary on the first bank with a broad pack-shaped plate. The related Mourner gate lies across the Bone Bridge on the other bank, so the props need a shared visual seal. Setting the pack down latches it; no simultaneous-player requirement.','ossuary'),
 ('Reliquary stair and loft access','Reliquary stair on the tower side with a deliberately authored rail drop into the Belfry loft route. Distinct brass shelf forms and broken rail silhouette; show the safe intended landing clearly.','reliquary'),
 ('Salt Mill above the canal','Salt Mill at+5m: oversized octagonal grinding drum and a broad white-salt chute over a low-poly storage room. A small opening looks back over canal landmarks so elevation stays readable.','mill'),
 ('Brine Larder canal cellar','Brine Larder at-2.5m, brining vat and drying racks against cool canal light seeping through a slit. Clear preparation bench and pack plinth; warm human-sized task island in a dark larger shell.','larder'),
 ('Cistern bank chamber','Cistern at-2.5m with one readable shallow basin, shore-side pots and a rim path. Indicate which bank the doorway returns to through distinct hoist-versus-bell silhouettes in distant openings.','cistern'),
 ('Canal rim wayfinding','A player walking the canal rim can see hoist and bell tower as two distinct silhouettes. Use brass hoist hooks on one bank and hanging bell cloth on the other; matching route marks work without relying on color alone.','rimE'),
 ('Pit vault and scout exit','Pit at-5m below the banks, compact vault mouth and one earned scout ladder/closet shortcut. The return sightline reconnects to the canal/Well, preserving the underground-to-bank distinction.','lair')],
 'D':[
 ('Arrival nave leading line','Arrival Hall into a long straight nave at0m whose leading line ends in the hoist over the Well. Tall simple ribs and one broad warm light at the far end; side chambers remain dark beads on two loops.','hall'),
 ('The Well pinch','The Well is the shared pinch through which both loops pass; bridge above at+2.5m and hoist to the north. Distinct mouths can be read from a low player view. No extra bypass doorway that changes topology.','rimN'),
 ('West Terrace wide room','West Terrace at0m is WIDE: horizontal stone benches, a broad low opening and roots visible through a wall break. Compose a strong contrast after a narrower connector, without cluttering the walkable floor.','terrace'),
 ('Cistern round flooded bead','Cistern at-2.5m is ROUND and FLOODED: a polygonal basin fills the chamber, with a readable rim walk. One lamp reflected in still teal water and a clear door shape at the next join.','cistern'),
 ('Root Grotto low organic bead','Root Grotto at-2.5m is LOW and ORGANIC: broad bent root beams make a compressed ceiling, few angular fungus clusters, a lantern wedge beyond. Human passage remains legible and the pack-sized gap reads honestly.','grotto'),
 ('Charnel Court sunken hearth','Court at0m is WIDE with a small-1.5m sunken centre. Broad cooking-court pots, a distinctive low hearth silhouette and clear steps. It should not look like the round flooded Cistern.','court'),
 ('Ossuary long upper gallery','Ossuary at+2.5m is LONG: repeated pale shelf braces and an obvious far pack plate, looking across the bridge into a different bead. Direction comes from spacing and landmark framing, not noisy decals.','ossuary'),
 ('Smokehouse tall tower','Smokehouse at+5m is TALL: one vertical chimney and hanging broad food racks, orange smoke shaft, dark upper void. A simple visual rhythm makes the room identifiable even in a small torch circle.','smokehouse'),
 ('Chime Hall long rhythm','Chime Hall at0m uses three heavy bells and a catwalk reached from the bridge gallery; low arches frame a long resonant space. The barred ladder and its higher lever read as a connected physical assembly.','chime'),
 ('Pump Room machine bead','Pump Room at-2.5m is MACHINE: one enormous wheel, square piston and dry channel pointing toward the sump stair. A single bright mechanism edge is enough; keep most surfaces dark and broad.','pump'),
 ('Salt Cellar low bead','Salt Cellar at-2.5m is LOW: chunky salt shelves, squat jars and a visible hand-wheel that relates to the Pump floor channel. Door thresholds squeeze then release the view as distinct beads.','cellar'),
 ('Pit cavern below the rings','Pit at-5m is CAVERN: broad black roof and a warm floor island, giant tracks, ladder toward a closet shortcut and the heavier Vault mouth. Convey the depth under the rings without adding a new opening.','lair')]
}
for variant,entries in zones.items():
    layout=layouts['v8'+variant.lower()]
    for i,(title,brief,room) in enumerate(entries,1):
        add('environment-'+variant,'ENV'+variant,i,title,
            f"Layout {variant}: {layout['notes']['thesis']} Specific place: {brief}",
            f"Attached layout v8{variant.lower()}, room/anchor {room}. Left is art direction; right is a dark player-height interpretation of the same place. Topology is a constraint, not a redesign.",ENV,
            layout='v8'+variant.lower(),room=room)

intros=[
 ('The last spoonful','01 an enormous nearly empty royal banquet table;02 King Cloche taps his spoon with a disappointed eye-squint;03 the Majordomo unfurls an absurdly long daily dish order;04 four tiny cooks receive a battered cookbook and shared pack;05 Bell Page rings beside the service lift;06 cut into first-person lantern view descending into the Well. A quiet visual punchline: one lonely herb sits on the royal plate.','A direct reusable court-to-expedition opening with no required voice exposition.'),
 ('The runaway royal order','01 a fresh wax-sealed order lands in a pantry;02 the scroll unrolls downhill past surprised cooks;03 Bell Page chases it through service doors;04 the crew catches it against the lift grate;05 the huge royal cloche crown is glimpsed through an upstairs hatch;06 the paper rolls neatly into the cookbook as the player steps into the dark descent.','A prop-comedy handoff keeps the story legible through action.'),
 ('A letter at the bunk','01 first-person chef mittens wake at a little workbench;02 a royal wax seal on a parchment invitation;03 matching inset views show King Cloche waiting at breakfast;04 the MajorDomo points from a dish silhouette to the downward stair;05 the player takes a cookbook and lantern;06 the real first-person door opens into the arrival nave.','An intimate first-person alternative requiring few cinematic camera setups.'),
 ('Beneath the banquet table','01 tiny chef-eye view under the royal table, giant shoes and rolling crumbs;02 a spoon drops with a thunderous comic ring;03 the Royal Taster notices an unfamiliar truffle aroma;04 a service hatch below the table reveals the pantry depth;05 Majordomo hands the scrappy crew a single recipe card;06 camera follows lantern light into a low service passage.','Scale comedy links the royal feast above with the overlooked undercity below.'),
 ('The lift passes the whole kingdom','01 royal table and cloche crown at the very top of a vertical service shaft;02 the order card clipped to the hoist basket;03 four cooks squeeze around a shared pack in the lift;04 elegant brass becomes repaired kitchen timber as the lift descends;05 warm court light shrinks above;06 player-height doors open onto a dark landing with the hoist still visible.','The lift explains vertical geography and introduces the hoist as a landmark.'),
 ('The accidental appointment','01 the Majordomo walks past a line of immaculately posed cooks;02 a scrappy small chef spills a harmless puff of flour;03 the Royal Taster tastes the accidental mixture and raises a spoon;04 King Cloche points at the surprised crew;05 a battered cookbook and ridiculous pack are ceremonially presented;06 the crew opens the underground service door.','A comic origin for unlikely royal cooks without requiring a combat tutorial.'),
 ('A court portrait comes alive','01 a flat cut-paper royal portrait fills frame;02 the cloche crown tilts and ivory eyes blink;03 the frame becomes the actual dining hall with a conspicuously empty bowl;04 MajorDomo pins the daily order beneath the frame;05 Bell Page guides the cooks past the picture into the service corridor;06 the painted doorway transforms into the real first-person dungeon entrance.','A stylized transition that can lean on graphic assets and a small set.'),
 ('The lost aroma','01 Royal Taster lifts a cloche and finds perfectly arranged but aroma-less food;02 a tiny visible amber scent curl escapes toward a floor grate;03 King Cloche sniffs with exaggerated anticipation;04 the Taster points a herb sprig toward the undercity order diagram;05 cooks pack a cookbook and jars, Bell Page opens the lift;06 lantern light catches the first huge truffle silhouette below.','An optional scent-led mystery; treats aroma as a visual storytelling idea rather than new canon.'),
 ('Bell Page delivery round','01 the little teal Bell Page rings through a sleepy service hall;02 each cook peeks from a different kitchen door;03 he gathers the four under the royal noticeboard;04 the Majordomo stamps a simple daily dish silhouette;05 one cook shoulders the oversized pack while the others take tools;06 the Bell Page stops at the threshold and waves the crew down into darkness.','An ensemble introduction with an obvious transition from safe home to expedition.'),
 ('The torn royal recipe','01 a royal recipe page has a conspicuous missing middle;02 the Taster compares its dish drawing with the royal empty bowl;03 King Cloche points to a familiar small food symbol on an old tile;04 the Majordomo gives the cooks the repaired cookbook with a question-mark patch;05 the crew matches the tile symbol to a service door;06 first-person lantern reveals a corresponding mark in the dungeon.','A knowledge-recovery opening; missing recipe content stays a proposed narrative device.'),
 ('The daily feast ritual','01 an enormous kitchen clock chimes beside a modest empty bowl;02 the court performs a silly synchronized cloche lift;03 King Cloche finds the expected dish missing;04 MajorDomo calmly replaces yesterday\'s order with today\'s parchment;05 four cooks trade looks and grab the familiar pack;06 the lift opens to the changing dark expedition. Do not show a gameplay countdown timer.','Establishes a repeating daily service without promising a timed expedition system.'),
 ('The pop-up feast book','01 a simple paper cloche opens into a cut-paper banquet court;02 hinged paper King and MajorDomo stand up;03 a daily dish sticker lands on the page;04 the next spread unfolds into hoist, bell tower and cooking stations;05 paper cooks walk toward a cutout door with their pack;06 the paper door fills frame and becomes a first-person low-poly dungeon door.','The cookbook itself bridges lore and play; paper animation is a distinct production option.')]
for i,(title,brief,notes) in enumerate(intros,1):add('intro','IN',i,title,brief,notes,INTRO)

huds=[
 ('Kitchen ticket rail','Slim overlapping cream kitchen order tickets on a horizontal top-left rail; party icons below; tiny torn-ticket notification centre-top; stamped keycap hints. Thin olive rules and large black ingredient silhouettes.','Compact ticket system with clear collection/preparation/return grouping.'),
 ('Pinned parchment corners','Dish objective is a small pinned upper-right paper, four chef portraits are separate thumb-sized corner cards upper-left; narrow note notification below the horizon; lower hints on little taped scraps. Expose most of the world.','Separated corners keep the centre and lower hand space open.'),
 ('Apron stitch ribbon','Parchment panels have two or three oversized apron stitches and a muted green cloth edge. Party health/voice states sit on simple hanging tabs; dish phases on one short horizontal stitched strip. No dense ornament.','A repair-and-craft visual language matching the physical cookbook and pack.'),
 ('Chalk marks on ivory','Very flat ivory paper with bold charcoal grease-pencil strokes, circles and ingredient doodles. Party rows use simple round silhouette stickers; voice activity is two thick expanding ink curves. One red alert underline.','Few colors and large marks; notification shape changes as well as color.'),
 ('The little service ledger','One compact ledger margin at the left: four party rows, then a small active dish line with three ingredient icons. Page fold reveals the expanded objective only in the lower component study. Quiet bottom item tabs.','An expandable ledger approach keeps the resting HUD modest.'),
 ('Hanging pantry tags','Cream hanging tag silhouettes with brass eyelets and short twine suggestions. Party portraits use square ingredient tags; dish tracker uses a long ticket with icon stamps; notification is a small torn label, not a giant banner.','Tags create hierarchy through silhouette; avoid dangling motion across the aiming area.'),
 ('Folded napkin cards','Soft geometric folded napkin corners and flat parchment colour, no realistic fabric. Objective a neat folded square, party a horizontal four-portrait strip with tiny microphone notches, contextual prompt a single folded key tab.','A gentler banquet-table option with broad calm shapes.'),
 ('Royal rubber stamps','Royal service stamp language with one restrained red wax circle, charcoal dish silhouette, olive checks, ivory square party portraits. Notification receives a little bell stamp. No elaborate heraldry.','Royal Feast branding expressed with simple repeatable stamp assets.'),
 ('Pictogram pantry','Extremely spare picture-first HUD: objective ingredient circles connected by three thick phase marks, party chefs as simple eye-and-hat silhouettes, voice waves visible as broad white marks, big clean parchment key tabs.','A low-text option; icons need an external naming/legend pass before production.'),
 ('Torn kitchen newspaper','Black hand-set slab lettering on cream torn strips, small halftone patches, sharp rectangular hierarchy. Party tracker resembles four small column mastheads; notification is a narrow news flash slip.','A graphic print option; torn edges stay peripheral to text.'),
 ('Twine and wax service kit','One olive twine line visually groups objective scraps, restrained red wax seal means new notification, party tabs hang off a short invisible rail. Calm flat cream fill and fat black icon strokes.','A tactile royal order motif; twine is decoration and never substitutes for a readable state icon.'),
 ('Quiet single-sheet HUD','The most minimal option: almost-flat ivory rectangles, gently asymmetric hand-cut corners, charcoal icons and sage progress marks. One-line objective, four tiny party icons with speaking/muted indicators, concise context prompt and very small item slots.','A baseline for lowest visual clutter; essential state differences still use shape and labels.')]
for i,(title,brief,notes) in enumerate(huds,1):add('hud','HUD',i,title,brief,notes,HUD)

mechanisms=[
 ('Fractured seal recipe slab','A squat stone tablet broken into TWO physically matching halves. Joining the halves restores three ordered kitchen glyphs. A corner notch and one asymmetrical border fix the reading orientation. Show one missing half, a found half on a shelf, joined slab, and the matching three-dial receiver. Clear direction uses carved arrows; obscure direction uses a chipped spoon groove.','Two-piece clue proposal for the existing ordered seal/dial read; not a new mandatory two-player task.'),
 ('Broken copper serving plate','Two crescent fragments of an oxidized copper serving plate fit into a shallow wooden holder. Three stamped food symbols become readable only when the plate is whole. Distinct rivet hole gives orientation; show the same marks on a nearby receiver.','A lighter carryable alternative to a stone slab, using the same fragment-reconstruction idea.'),
 ('Charcoal rubbing scraps','A worn wall relief can be understood using two large paper rubbings that line up at a broad torn edge. One rubbing shows positions, the other restores a missing glyph. Show the cook hand holding paper under lantern light and a combined page clue.','A cookbook-compatible clue delivery option; proposed interaction, not an existing tool feature.'),
 ('Hanging feast plate order','Three large ceramic plates hang at visibly different heights, each with a huge distinct kitchen symbol. A broken plate fragment supplies a missing ordering mark. Clear version uses thick incised slots; obscure version uses repeating table-setting marks.','Sequence communicated through spatial arrangement rather than tiny written text.'),
 ('Bellkeeper chipped relief','A three-glyph relief on the Well wall or Bell Tower face is chipped in two places. A found stone shard restores the sequence. Show the intentional reading angle from a bridge/other bank and the same symbols on chunky rotary dials.','Grounded in P4: clue visible from an authored vantage; preserve the existing dial interaction.'),
 ('Shadow stencil halves','Two broken stamped tin stencils slot into a lantern bracket and cast three simple symbol silhouettes onto a nearby flat wall. Large alignment notch prevents ambiguous rotation. Show unaligned and aligned states under the same warm light.','An optional new shadow-clue treatment; would require a deliberate implementation decision.'),
 ('Roots around the old waymarks','Broad roots partly obscure old directional slab marks. A bright visible notch indicates an important junction; a subtler version uses root growth and repeated spoon-shapes toward an optional cache. Show player eye views of both readable and obscure interpretations.','Keep mandatory route hints clearer than optional treasure hints.'),
 ('Brine channel tells the mechanism','A floor channel physically leads from a broad wheel to a barred sump stair or Chain Crossing. Dry/puddled channel and slack/taut chain are separate visible states. Show before/after mechanical movement and a close player-level direction tell.','Grounded in P2. The trace should explain the cause/effect rather than become decorative piping.'),
 ('Quarry cuts and kitchen marks','A family of three chunky chisel marks on stone door jambs: return-to-hoist hook, bell-bank bell, pantry spoon. Show crisp high-contrast marks for the main route and nearly erased shallow marks toward an optional detour.','Shape-plus-placement wayfinding; a color-blind player can use the same marks.'),
 ('The shared-pack plinth','Broad stone plate with a simple pack-shaped depression, stitched sack icon and matching receiver seal on the distant gate. Show empty, pack placed, and gate visibly latched open. Clear handprint wear indicates where to put the pack.','Grounded in P3: one set-down action latches the gate; no simultaneous hold requirement.'),
 ('Backside bar and earned shortcut','A barred closet door has a completely readable heavy bar on the far side. One-way scout ladder reveals the bar and a chunky lever. Before/after views show the newly connected return route; scratch arrows differ on the two sides.','Grounded in SC2: discovery and opening are readable; avoid implying the locked side already opens.'),
 ('The far key in the window','A small red key-shaped silhouette on a warm lit plinth can be seen from far across the Well; the lower Vault has a large matching red-and-key-shaped socket. Show near/far relationship and one subtle sightline framing variant. For B preserve the15m elevation separation.','Grounded in P1. Distinct shape accompanies red so the link is not color-only.')]
for i,(title,brief,notes) in enumerate(mechanisms,1):add('mechanisms','MECH',i,title,brief,notes,MECHANISM)

monsters=[
 ('Long Widow','A tiny pale faceted body suspended high near the ceiling on eight absurdly long angular legs. Legs reach around doorway edges BEFORE the body floats through. A few ivory eye points remain high in darkness. Gentle stone tapping and scraped dust mark its route. No bulky tarantula body.','Trigger: a nearby clatter. Response: slowly probe its last location, pause, then resume patrol. Counter: stop moving, wait for the legs/body to clear, use another route. Existing crawler direction; never permanently block the only exit.'),
 ('Pickle Mimic','One large angular green pickle inside a squat intact glass jar, black face and two ivory eyes hidden until it tilts. The lid clicks before it shuffles. A tiny brine ring marks a resting spot. Show quiet jar, lid tell, revealed mimic, and a whole-jar-preserving player approach.','Trigger: a close loud sound. Response: turn toward sound and make one short shuffle/lunge. Counter: bait the sound then approach while it settles; preserve the jar. Prototype-friendly existing creature direction.'),
 ('Cauldron Slime','A broad simple soup jelly spilling from a battered black pot, two floating ingredient eye shapes, one thick syrup trail. Its silhouette is pot plus one wobbling mass, not a detailed tentacle monster. Warm light subtly brightens its simmering core.','Trigger: approaching a warm light. Response: slowly follow the nearest warm source, pause when it cools. Counter: route it around a table or leave a light source away from the ingredient path. Simple proposed lure loop.'),
 ('Bread Crab','A little crusty round loaf shell with four chunky bread-stick legs and ivory eye slots below the crust. A loud dry crackle precedes one sideways scuttle. Breadcrumb trail and a snapped crust flake show where it passed.','Trigger: dropped crumbs. Response: approach, grab one crumb, retreat to its nook. Counter: place the lure away from the route and pass while it feeds. Proposed simple foraging threat.'),
 ('Marrow Knight','A squat stack of huge simplified soup bones around a dark hollow torso, one oversized arm bone and a small brass ladle-like shield. Two tiny warm eyes peer from a shallow bowl helmet. Bone taps and chalky dust footprints, no anatomical gore.','Trigger: metal clang. Response: turn and take several heavy steps toward it, then wait. Counter: lure it beyond a pillar and pass behind its slow turn. Harvest preservation remains a separate future feature.'),
 ('Bellied Pilgrim','Tall narrow faceless kitchen pilgrim with a comically round hanging cooking-pot belly and bent knees. One amber eye slit above an apron. Pot-belly rumble and a little spilled bean line signal its slow route. Broad cloth planes, few joints.','Trigger: sustained nearby movement noise. Response: pause, face the sound, then lumber to the last position. Counter: stop before it faces you and use the other side of a broad room. No door camping forever.'),
 ('Knuckleback','A low wide root-and-stone creature with two enormous front knuckles and a small head tucked between shoulder plates. No realistic skin. One knuckle taps the ground before it pivots; a pair of rubbed stone streaks trails behind it.','Trigger: a heavy nearby floor impact. Response: pivot toward the impact and advance a short distance. Counter: bait a floor clatter off-route and cross its slow rear side. Proposed cheap impact-investigation loop.'),
 ('Root Listener','A mostly stationary root bundle in a corner, with two pale seed eyes buried in a faceted bulb. Thin roots twitch toward the last noise; loose soil falls first. A root-ring scrape on the floor shows its reach. Distinct from a humanoid chef.','Trigger: noise inside a short radius. Response: reach one root toward the source then retract. Counter: pause, step beyond the clearly shown reach, or distract from outside it. One readable hazard cycle.'),
 ('Pantry Porter','A tall narrow covered serving trolley on four little bent legs, dark face visible under one cloche lip. One hanging spoon gives a soft clink before it rolls. A flour wheel-track is its trace; silhouette is rectangular and top-heavy.','Trigger: a visible moving player in a short front cone. Response: slowly follow until a corner breaks sight, then return to its pantry route. Counter: use broad shelves to break line of sight. No permanent threshold blocking.'),
 ('Rag Maw','A low hanging bundle of angular apron scraps below a shelf, a black triangular mouth and two button-like ivory eyes. It looks like harmless laundry at rest; fabric lifts and inhales before one short snap. A dragged lint seam marks its hang point.','Trigger: loud close footsteps. Response: one inhale/snap/recover cycle without a long chase. Counter: stop at the inhaling tell, then cross during recovery. Proposed short-range ambush with a clear tell.'),
 ('Wax Wisp','A squat lumpy candle-wax creature carrying one dim wick, dark face under a wax hood and two ivory pin eyes. It leaves large wax droplets and a tiny wick hiss. Broad polygon lumps, no smoke-particle overload.','Trigger: a nearby lamp goes dark. Response: drift slowly toward that last dark point and wait briefly. Counter: keep a light between it and the route or pass during its wait. Proposed light-state investigation, not an instant punishment.'),
 ('Brine Hog','A short barrel-shaped brined-root boar with jar-lid shoulder plates, a huge square snout and two soft ivory eyes. A wet snuffle and salt flecks precede a short push. Heavy simple hoof prints, teal brine shine as broad patches.','Trigger: a loose food scent/lure nearby. Response: sniff, approach slowly, nudge once, settle. Counter: leave optional bait off the travel line and pass while it noses it. One short lure loop; no complex charging combat.')]
for i,(title,brief,notes) in enumerate(monsters,1):add('monsters','MON',i,title,brief+' Behavior to depict: '+notes,notes,MONSTER)

vermin=[
 ('Crumb foragers','All four are sweet small pantry scavengers. Rat has an angular bread-crumb saddle; sootling nudges a crust; flour puff rolls a tiny crumb; lint scuttler drags a biscuit corner. Quiet low silhouettes and a shared feeding cluster.','Role: ambience and optional crumb feeding. No stolen quest items; they retreat from a close player.'),
 ('Tiny noise makers','Rat drags a small stolen fork with a harmless clink, sootling rattles loose charcoal, flour puff sneezes one broad flour cloud, lint scuttler drags a noisy tin button. Show the tiny objects and clear pre-noise anticipation.','Role: optional stealth disturbance. A visible anticipation pose comes before the sound; no surprise unavoidable alarm.'),
 ('Lamp and warmth followers','Sootling huddles beside a warm lamp, flour puff backs away into a cool shelf shadow, rat follows the edge of the light pool, lint scuttler carries one glowing amber fibre. Four clearly different body silhouettes.','Role: environmental warmth cues and ambience. Their responses help read light without making them mandatory tools.'),
 ('Little pantry thieves','Rat carries only a loose crumb, sootling steals a charcoal chip, flour puff rolls a fallen bread cube, lint scuttler pulls a scrap of wrapping. Tiny tug-of-war poses against overlarge food props.','Role: optional harmless interaction with loose scraps. Never take a required expedition ingredient or key.'),
 ('Guides through the small gaps','Rat slips under a shelf gap, sootling peeks from a warm vent, flour puff drifts with a draft, lint scuttler leaves a broad thread pointing through a crack. The player can see each tiny departure route.','Role: hint at existing crawls/vents and optional nooks; do not create new traversable links.'),
 ('Sleepy kitchen residents','Rat asleep in a folded napkin, sootling curled beside cold ash, flour puff gently compressed beneath a bowl edge, lint scuttler tucked into a tied rag. Large soft expressive shapes rendered with flat facets.','Role: pure ambience. Players may look or gently startle them; no resource or navigation requirement.'),
 ('A small startle cascade','Rat hops and drops a teaspoon, sootling puffs a single ember-free dust burst, flour puff sneezes, lint scuttler scurries under a pot. Show three tiny motion beats then the calm hiding cluster.','Role: optional readable noise chain. Keep it local and predictable; no unavoidable lethal monster summon.'),
 ('The pantry cleaning crew','Rat eats crumbs, sootling absorbs ash, flour puff gathers loose flour into itself, lint scuttler bundles thread. The four distinct creature bodies visibly tidy a tiny patch of mess.','Role: ambience that explains traces and clean patches. Could support a simple feed/watch interaction without a new economy.'),
 ('Harmless eyes in the dark','Four very small eye-height pairs under a low shelf reveal the four cute bodies when a lamp reaches them: pointed rat ears, coal spikes, flour cloud and rag fringe. A larger empty doorway remains a separate unknown shape.','Role: atmospheric false alarm with a fair size cue. Harmless creatures should not use the exact danger tell of a lethal monster.'),
 ('The crumb-led scout','Rat follows a crumb line to an existing hole, sootling points its little body toward warmth, flour puff is tugged by air, lint scuttler catches a loose thread on a hidden shelf edge. A chef mitten offers a tiny crumb.','Role: optional scouting hint and light interaction. A route stays solvable without understanding the vermin.'),
 ('Curious jar visitors','A wide open empty jar lies on its side; rat sniffs, sootling sits beside it, flour puff squeezes in like a soft cloud, lint scuttler decorates the rim with thread. Show an open hand and safe release pose.','Role: optional catch-and-release play proposal. No mandatory capture, harm or cooking these small companions.'),
 ('Herb and paper couriers','Rat has a loose rosemary sprig, sootling carries a paprika-colored scrap, flour puff wears a fallen paper chef-hat fold, lint scuttler drags a twine bow. Tiny silhouette accents create charming individual identities.','Role: visual flavor and optional curiosity. Carried scraps are incidental, not critical recipe materials.')]
for i,(title,brief,notes) in enumerate(vermin,1):add('vermin','VER',i,title,brief,notes,VERMIN)

